    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="d163-01" n="1" xml:id="d163-01"/>

                <head>163. Notes of Telephone Conversation Between the President’s Assistant for
                    National Security Affairs (Kissinger) and the British Ambassador
                        (Tomkins)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d163-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d163-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1969-11-24T19:55:00-05:00">November 24, 1969, 7:55 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p> K wanted to tell T now, on a personal basis that we are going to make an
                    announcement tomorrow about our policy with regard to biological and chemical
                    warfare. K said we are going to endorse the principles of the United Kingdom
                    draft convention. And we will offer to work out specific provisions with you. T
                    asked if we would announce the last part. K said yes. K asked that T make sure
                    the Prime Minister knows; K asked that he handle it on a personal basis between
                    the President and the Prime Minister. T said he would and that he was most
                    grateful to K.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d163-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d163-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Library of Congress, Manuscript Division, Kissinger Papers, Box 361,
                    Telephone Conversations, Chronological File, 18–28 November 1969. No
                    classification marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d163-f2" n="2" xml:id="d163-f2-content">
                <p> Kissinger informed Tomkins about the decision to be announced the next day
                    concerning chemical and biological weapons.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
